{
  "id": "pi67ksk",
  "title": "Chapter 6: Sound",
  "order": 55,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6m9zyxh",
      "content": "Sound is a form of mechanical energy that produces the sensation of hearing. It is produced due to vibrations of objects and travels through a medium in the form of sound waves. Sound is essential for communication, music and many scientific applications."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Audible Range",
          "value": "20 Hz - 20 kHz",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
