    {
      "id": "6hitoro",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Sound"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Sound is a longitudinal mechanical wave that requires a material medium to propagate and cannot travel in a vacuum.",
        "Loudness of sound depends on the amplitude of vibration, whereas pitch depends on the frequency.",
        "An echo is formed by the reflection of sound and requires a minimum distance of 17.2 meters between the source and obstacle.",
        "Ultrasound has frequencies higher than 20,000 Hz and is widely used in medical imaging, SONAR, and industrial cleaning.",
        "The speed of sound is highest in solids, moderate in liquids, and lowest in gases."
      ],
      "id": "n59ouqw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kluz43k",
      "content": "• Sound is a form of energy that produces the sensation of hearing."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cufh4m0",
      "content": "• It is produced by vibrating objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ddop7n1",
      "content": "• Sound travels through a medium in the form of waves."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tnlopna",
      "content": "• It cannot travel through vacuum because it requires a material medium."
    },
    {
      "id": "vm1d6r3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Production of Sound"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vnq3j71",
      "content": "• Sound is produced when an object vibrates."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s3wfvnn",
      "content": "• The vibrating object causes nearby particles of the medium to vibrate."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g0s6rnl",
      "content": "• These vibrations travel through the medium as sound waves."
    },
    {
      "id": "5m1c1cc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Sound Waves"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xg9onsp",
      "content": "Sound waves are longitudinal waves consisting of compressions and rarefactions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s6jozsf",
      "content": "• Compression – region of high pressure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nfucz01",
      "content": "• Rarefaction – region of low pressure."
    },
    {
      "id": "e8bohl6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Characteristics of Sound Waves"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Sound requires a material medium like solid, liquid, or gas for its propagation and cannot travel through a vacuum.",
      "id": "fjlq0v2"
    },
    {
      "id": "ta9bge8",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Characteristic</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Amplitude</p>",
            "<p>Maximum displacement of particles; determines loudness</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Frequency</p>",
            "<p>Number of vibrations per second</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Wavelength</p>",
            "<p>Distance between two compressions</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Time Period</p>",
            "<p>Time taken for one complete vibration</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fu2b171",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Types of Sound"
    },
    {
      "id": "w4ij5ww",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
