          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Infrasonic</p>",
            "<p>Less than 20 Hz</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Audible Sound</p>",
            "<p>20 Hz – 20,000 Hz</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ultrasonic</p>",
            "<p>Greater than 20,000 Hz</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lrw01ks",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Speed of Sound"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aud6ne6",
      "content": "The speed of sound depends on the medium and temperature. It travels fastest in solids and slowest in gases."
    },
    {
      "id": "snhnzbm",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Medium</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Speed</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Air</p>",
            "<p>343 m/s</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Water</p>",
            "<p>1500 m/s</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Steel</p>",
            "<p>5000 m/s</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b2deo2u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Reflection of Sound"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b0tsm2a",
      "content": "When sound waves strike a surface, they bounce back. This phenomenon is called reflection of sound."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Parameter",
